  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Carahsoft Technology recorded $1.4B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Carahsoft Technology received 1,409 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $974K. Obligations fell 24.1% year over year. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $654M, followed by the Department of Health and Human Services at $230M and the Department of Homeland Security at $109M. Software Publishers is the largest market by NAICS, with $956M in obligations, followed by Other Computer Related Services at $211M and a second Software Publishers category at $109M. Historical obligations show six years of activity: FY21 $1.2B, FY22 $1.3B, FY23 $1.4B, FY24 $1.8B, FY25 $1.8B, and FY26 $1.4B. The top buying agencies list also includes the Department of Agriculture at $97M, the General Services Administration at $65.6M, and the Social Security Administration at $59.8M. The NAICS breakdown shows additional categories including Custom Computer Programming Services at $64.4M, Electronic Computer Manufacturing at $19.6M, and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $8.7M.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies are buying the most from Carahsoft Technology?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the top buyer, obligating $654M. The Department of Health and Human Services follows with $230M, and the Department of Homeland Security follows with $109M. Other buyers in the top ten include the Department of Agriculture at $97M and the General Services Administration at $65.6M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What products and markets dominate Carahsoft Technology's federal work?",
        "body": "Software Publishers is the dominant market, accounting for $956M in obligations. Other Computer Related Services accounts for $211M, and Custom Computer Programming Services accounts for $64.4M. The NAICS list also shows Electronic Computer Manufacturing at $19.6M, Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $8.7M, Computing Infrastructure Providers at $2.1M, and small categories at $237K, $199K, and $190K."
      }
    ]
  },
